+# The Galaxy S25+ (SM-S936B) port
+
+The S25+ is a sibling target to the base S25 documented in [s25.md](s25.md). The OneiOS guest, XNU host, image,
+Adreno bridge and Oryon CPU plan are shared; this device's native panel is QHD+ (1440x3120 at up to 120 Hz),
+instead of the base S25's FHD+ (1080x2340). The device codename is `pa2q`. This port is **prepared but not yet
+run on an S25+**. Hardware facts below are specifications or expectations until the probe has been run on the phone.
+
+| Area | S25+ expectation | Port handling |
+|---|---|---|
+| Model | SM-S936B (regional variants use SM-S936*) | The [companion OneOS app](https://github.com/akshaynexus/OneOS/blob/oneios/app-android/core/model/src/main/kotlin/com/fahadali/oneos/core/model/Profiles.kt) already has an S25+ profile matching `SM-S936*` + `pa2q` + `SM8750` (`S_PLUS_8750`). |
+| SoC / CPU | Snapdragon 8 Elite for Galaxy, SM8750; Oryon 2 prime + 6 performance cores | A companion OneOS probe identifies this S25+ as SM8750. The OneiOS probe still confirms the exact running handset's MIDR, capacities, frequency tables and core count. |
+| GPU | Adreno 830 | Same KGSL / drm2kgsl path as the base S25. Probe `chip_id`, `gpu_id`, import and submit on this handset. |
+| Panel | 1440x3120, QHD+, adaptive up to 120 Hz | The takeover display helper asks SurfaceFlinger for the panel's largest native mode, and xnuhost uses the reported mode. At scale 3 this gives 480x1040 guest points; scale 2 gives 720x1560. A frame is about 17.97 MiB. |
+| Firmware, kernel, root and HALs | Not measured on this handset | Use the probe output. Do not assume the base S25's exact firmware or HAL details. |
+
+The OneiOS manager previously hid its system card on this profile. Its companion source now includes
+`S_PLUS_8750` in `OneiosSystem.PROFILE_IDS`, so the card is offered for this phone and shows the existing experimental
+confirmation. Build and install that updated manager before expecting OneiOS to appear in the app.
+
+## What is shared and what is different
+
+No separate XNU board, kernel profile, guest image, or GPU implementation is required for the S25+. Both S25 models
+use the same hosted architecture and the S25+ stays within the existing 1440x3120 display limits. The SurfaceFlinger
+mode report is already used in takeover sessions, so it selects the S25+'s actual native dimensions and refresh rate;
+the configured or reported mode takes precedence over the base S25 fallback. If the display helper cannot read modes
+and the runtime cannot read a connected panel mode, the compiled fallback is still the base S25's 1080x2340. In that
+case, provide the native dimensions with `--width 1440 --height 3120` or resolve the display mode reporting first.
+
+The companion OneOS profile is based on an S25+ probe, but OneiOS-specific runtime support still needs a probe and
+session on the target handset. The OneiOS probe is the same read-only hardware survey as the S25 probe, with a
+separate archive name so results stay distinct. Run it with One UI active and root granted:
+
+```sh
+adb push tools/probe/s25-probe.sh /data/local/tmp/
+adb shell su -c 'sh /data/local/tmp/s25-probe.sh s25-plus'
+```
+
+It writes `/data/local/tmp/oneios-s25-plus-probe-<time>.tar.gz`. The CPU, GPU, display, touch, haptics, battery,
+sensor, Bluetooth, audio, camera, kernel and SELinux results settle the remaining device-specific assumptions.
+
+## Validation status
+
+The display-mode test already exercises a 1440x3120 panel report, matching the S25+'s expected native size. That is
+a host-side check of sizing and frame allocation, not evidence of a successful OneiOS phone session. No OneiOS S25+
+GPU submission, boot, or return-to-One-UI session has been observed yet.
